00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:43.280
PLEASE DISMOUNT AND WALK
YOUR BIKE ACROSS THE BRIDGE{車轉自ラガナシ押 = push bike}

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.520
Hello, Akiaki-san!

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:50.420
<b>AKIAKI-SAN</b>

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:50.420
<b>(WEARY-WEARY){飽​き​飽​き}</b>

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.040
Hold on a second, Hachikuji.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.940
Don't greet me in a weary manner,

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.380
as though you're already sick of talking to me.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.950
My name is Araragi.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.800
Forgive me. I flubbed it.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.800
< kami - mashita >

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:02.390
No, that was on purpose.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:03.490
I fwubbed it!

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:03.490
< kami - mamita >

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.870
It wasn't on purpose?!

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:07.720
Araragi-san, where are you headed today?

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.440
As you can see, I'm on my way to school.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.280
I told you the other day, remember?

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.760
I've changed jobs from a delinquent slacker
to a serious high school student.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.880
That's why I'm going to school.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:23.200
Though, delinquent high school students also go to school.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.790
You know, Hachikuji,

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:27.980
there's something I need to tell you.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:29.450
What is it?

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:30.440
Oshino...

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:32.460
Oshino Meme...

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:37.150
that specialist old man who helped you and others, left this town.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.030
That was rather sudden.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:46.210
You never met him in person, so you may not care,

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:51.310
but you're not completely uninvolved,
so I thought you should at least know.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:56.060
But, Araragi-san, what happened to that one case?

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.660
That one case?

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:58.860
Which case do you mean?

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.240
Come on...

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.110
This one. This one!

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:07.340
Or is it easier if I put it this way, Araragi-san?

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:10.700
Good job evading your 5 million yen debt.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.460
I didn't evade it!

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:14.130
Listen up, Hachikuji.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.710
I'm a man who returns money I borrow.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.480
I finished paying Oshino off.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:22.700
I'm a clean man who finished paying off his debt.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.030
I see...

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.720
That's slightly disappointing.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:28.850
Why?

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.480
See, you mentioned it the other day.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:32.710
The other day?

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:37.370
I'm talking about when you were being stalked by that speedy underclassman.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:42.980
You consulted me, asking what you should do
about the huge debt you owed Oshino-san.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:47.530
And, during that consultation, you mentioned you didn't have to pay cash,

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:53.350
but if there were some uncommon apparition stories, you might be able to cash them in.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.880
Yeah... I may have said that.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.610
And so, Araragi-san, ever since then,

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:03.340
my unworthy self has been wondering if I could help you.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:07.350
I looked for a story of that nature while I was strolling around.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.330
Stories about apparitions, or something like ghost stories.

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:15.210
Y-You were doing that for me?

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:21.230
My plan to sell my painstakingly located stories to you for a high price is ruined!

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.490
Plan?

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.100
High price?

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:23.610
Huh?

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.610
They aren't free?

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.090
No way.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:32.420
Araragi-san, I won't say 5 million yen anymore, so please buy them!

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:34.350
Make me an offer!

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:39.320
Tell me, what's your asking price, Hachikuji Echigoya? {apparently a greedy merchant; Rokube Echigoya, Tenchu}

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.040
I'm fine with 50 yen.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.130
So cheap!

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:45.800
Well, it's only worth that much.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:49.910
You were trying to sell me something
worth 50 yen for 5 million?

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.790
So, what kind of a story is it? Let's hear it.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:54.780
Yes.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:57.290
Well, it's a tale of sand.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.310
Sand?

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.720
<i>It was, how to put it...</i>

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.240
<i>like a demon's face.</i>

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.040
<i>A bloodcurdling drawing.</i>

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.750
<i>The sand itself was like an apparition.</i>

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:25.240
<i>Hachikuji was strolling around looking for
strange or mysterious phenomena to sell to me.</i>

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:32.240
<i>So she might see something strange
in the surface of a normally trivial sandbox.</i>

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:39.500
<i>But, on different days, would the same
"demon's face" appear in the same way?</i>

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.770
<i>In other words, however much you change it,
however much you push it around,</i>

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:49.510
<i>the sand in this sandbox would revert to the shape of a demon.</i>

