00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:57.170
Oh, so there's another.

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:59.490
You really do know everything.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:01.560
I don't know everything.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.230
I only know what I know.

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.420
A third possibility.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:09.760
If it's not the actions of an apparition or a human,

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:11.850
then, let's see...

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:16.010
Well, when you think logically, using the process of elimination,

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:20.240
the only thing I can think of is a natural phenomenon.

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:23.890
HANEKAWA TSUBASA

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:23.890
HANEKAWA TSUBASA

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.500
<i>That's right.</i>

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.890
<i>You have a grasp of things, Araragi-kun.</i>

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.380
But a natural phenomenon?

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:28.630
Something like that can't possibly happen—{dash en –; dash em —}

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:31.130
You know, Araragi-kun...

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:34.760
Wind and rain aren't the only
natural phenomena out there, right?

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:41.280
<i>What you'd call an epilogue, or the punch line for this episode.</i>

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.020
You know, Araragi-kun...

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:47.060
You keep saying that you investigated the sandbox,

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:49.790
but you only checked the sand, right?

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:54.090
The box holding the sand is part of the sandbox, too.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:58.680
So, Araragi-kun, you claim to have investigated the sandbox,

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:03.230
but you can't claim that unless you investigated the box as well.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.710
Additionally, sand itself is heavy.

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.350
Even mundane, ordinary sand.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:14.440
<i>It was too obvious to even consider.</i>

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.360
<i>It was because the bottom of the sandbox had cracked,</i>

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:23.170
<i>likely deteriorating from age and what Hanekawa calls "the weight of sand."</i>

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:27.250
<i>The truth was that as a result,
the sand was settling in a pattern.</i>

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:32.260
<i>The fact that it was in the shape of a demon was, as expected, just a coincidence.</i>

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:38.220
<i>For now, it's just a natural phenomenon causing weird patterns in the sand.</i>

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:44.100
<i>But if the crack continues to grow,
the sandbox will no longer have a bottom,</i>

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.870
<i>and the sand and dirt will mix,</i>

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:49.390
<i>possibly causing quicksand or liquefaction.</i>

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:53.750
<i>Even though that's the worst case scenario,</i>

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:58.200
<i>playing in a broken box is dangerous enough.</i>

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.180
<i>Enough that every moment counts.</i>

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:03.940
<i>That's why Hanekawa scolded me.</i>

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:08.630
To start, I guess I should call park management.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:13.020
<i>The scariest thing, and the least peaceful,</i>

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:15.460
<i>wasn't an apparition or a human's action,</i>

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.070
<i>but seems to have been nature.</i>

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:20.950
<i>Scary like a demon,</i>

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:22.670
<i>and scary like a human.</i>

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:49.940
<b>Nayami ketobashite ishi ga korogatte ku</b>

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:49.940
<b>Kicking a stone as if I was kicking my troubles</b>

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:55.690
<b>Sukoshi gomakashita are wa shigatsu no koto</b>

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:55.690
<b>It was April when I played my trick</b>

00:10:55.900 --> 00:11:01.160
<b>Koukishin ousei de akarui kodomo deshita</b>

00:10:55.900 --> 00:11:01.160
<b>I was a curious and cheerful child</b>

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:06.910
<b>Senaka oshita no wa ano hi kara no boku de</b>

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:06.910
<b>The me from the past gave me a push</b>

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:12.790
<b>Hamidasenai retsu wo oinuite</b>

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:12.790
<b>Let's loiter on the way</b>

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:18.380
<b>Michikusa wo shiyou</b>

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:18.380
<b>Passing a line you can't even lean out from</b>

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:26.060
<b>Kago ni nose taisetsu na yume</b>

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:26.060
<b>I'll put my precious dreams in the basket</b>

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:31.440
<b>pedaru mawashi tooku made saa mochi dasou</b>

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:31.440
<b>and spin the pedals, carrying them far away!</b>

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:36.820
<b>Uwasa shita boku no mirai wa</b>

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:36.820
<b>My rumored future...</b>

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:38.610
<b>Kokochi iino?</b>

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:38.610
<b>Am I comfortable with it?</b>

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.900
<b>Nobiru kage ni kiitemo</b>

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:41.900
<b>I even asked my long shadow;</b>

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:50.750
<b>Wakaranai wakaranai wakaranai</b>

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:44.950
<b>It doesn't know a thing...</b>

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:47.700
<b>It doesn't know a thing...</b>

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:50.750
<b>It doesn't know a thing...</b>
